WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Luffy is SO GOOD with his devil fruit that it is&nbsp;
basically the only power he needs for the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.680
first half of the story. But then THIS HAPPENS,&nbsp;
and then THIS and he suddenly realizes that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:17.700
needs top tier haki similar to the likes Shanks or&nbsp;
Roger so that he can survive in the New World. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.920
THEN after seeing how overpowered he becomes&nbsp;
using haki in the second half of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.780
I just couldn’t stop wondering, how&nbsp;
strong Luffy COULD have been if he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:34.620
never ate his devil fruit at all and instead&nbsp;
had trained ONLY haki ever since he was a kid?

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.640
And this would most likely happen all the&nbsp;
way back when Luffy got his devil fruit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.880
Because let’s assume that the Red-Hair pirates&nbsp;
don’t completely lose track of the single most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:51.000
valuable devil fruit, so when hungry child&nbsp;
Luffy is looking around for something to eat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.880
Shanks keeps the treasure box with the devil&nbsp;
fruit out of his reach. And even though kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:04.260
Luffy is desperate to see what is in the box,&nbsp;
Shanks says no. So goodbye stretchy Luffy.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.740
But that’s not all that is different about his&nbsp;
back story, because even without his rubber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:13.380
abilities he’s still the impulsive kid we know&nbsp;
and love, so when he insults these bandits he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.840
still going to get captured, taken out to sea,&nbsp;
and has to be rescued by Shanks because even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:26.820
though he can now swim, he’s still no match for&nbsp;
this monstrous sea king. But now we get the NEXT&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:33.780
MAJOR twist because when they get back to land,&nbsp;
Luffy suddenly has A TON of questions about how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:40.080
Shanks scared away the sea king. Now since this&nbsp;
version of Luffy doesn’t have his devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:47.220
Shanks decides to show Luffy the very basics of&nbsp;
haki so he can grow strong and protect himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:54.240
And I’m talking specifically about armament and&nbsp;
observation haki here since Luffy hasn’t awakened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.940
his conqueror’s haki yet. Although I guess it&nbsp;
is possible that Shanks could assume that Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:05.880
has conquerors because of his dad and grandpa, so&nbsp;
he might even tell Luffy about all three powers.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:12.300
However, this is where we run into&nbsp;
our first major debate. Because when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.860
Shanks is about to depart in the original&nbsp;
story, he gives Luffy the straw hat as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:23.460
symbol of his belief in the young boy.&nbsp;
At least that’s what we always thought,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:31.680
but there is also the very real possibility that&nbsp;
Shanks only tried to inspire Luffy BECAUSE HE ATE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:38.220
this particular devil fruit. That’s because&nbsp;
this devil fruit is extra special and we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:46.080
only assume it is required in order to become Joy&nbsp;
Boy, which Luffy just managed to achieve in Wano.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:55.920
So the big question is, would Shanks still give&nbsp;
up his hat if Luffy doesn’t have the devil fruit?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:03.960
I’m honestly not sure, but I think that Luffy’s&nbsp;
personality would still inspire Shanks. Plus it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:10.680
is still possible for Luffy to find Laugh Tale and&nbsp;
become pirate king without becoming Joy Boy - I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:16.680
mean Roger did it - so let’s assume Luffy still&nbsp;
gets the hat and Shanks even tells him that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:23.580
might even tell him more about what was in that&nbsp;
treasure chest when Luffy becomes a great pirate.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:31.260
Which leaves us with the ABSOLUTE CRAZY SCENARIO&nbsp;
of Luffy growing up training his haki instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:37.320
his devil fruit powers. I mean can you imagine&nbsp;
him running around the Goa Kingdom blasting off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:44.160
haki punches?! He would be insanely strong! And&nbsp;
I honestly think his grandpa Garp would be SO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:50.340
HAPPY to see his Grandson learning haki&nbsp;
that he might even train Luffy himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:57.540
which ultimately means that Luffy’s fighting style&nbsp;
will be VERY SIMILAR to Garp’s where he mainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:06.060
fights with his fists. Although I suppose there&nbsp;
is a decent chance Luffy might eventually learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:11.520
to use a weapon since most haki-only powerhouses&nbsp;
like Roger and Shanks use a weapon as well.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:20.760
In fact, I HAVE THE PERFECT WEAPON for Haki Luffy&nbsp;
to use which we’ll discuss a little later on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.740
but first Luffy would probably also awaken his&nbsp;
conqueror’s haki during his time growing up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:31.380
perhaps when he was captured by bandits&nbsp;
or maybe when Sabo “died”. Which means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.540
that by the time Luffy is ready to start his&nbsp;
pirate adventure his haki skill has leveled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:44.100
up from noob to master and he’s basically&nbsp;
at the same level he was right after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:50.940
timeskip. But we’ll see VERY SOON how long&nbsp;
he can survive without his devil fruit.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.860
What you may not even realize though is that&nbsp;
not having a devil fruit is actually going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.860 --> 00:05:01.500
save his life more than once in the East Blue.&nbsp;
Because while most of the enemies in this part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:06.840
of the story were fairly easy to beat, you&nbsp;
may have forgotten that Rubber Luffy almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:12.180
drowned TWICE! Once when he was thrown off the&nbsp;
Baratie and once when he dropped into the water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:18.420
like an anchor while fighting Arlong. Both&nbsp;
times he had to be saved by others, but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:24.360
is no longer a problem because this version&nbsp;
of Luffy has no restrictions with swimming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:30.420
so defeating his enemies becomes a simple problem&nbsp;
of smashing their faces with his haki-covered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:37.020
kicks and punches. Plus his observation haki will&nbsp;
help him dodge attacks like Arlong’s spinning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:42.300
torpedo and he would even be able to easily&nbsp;
break weapons with his haki-infused attacks.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:49.020
But the most insane part of Luffy’s new abilities&nbsp;
is that he would definitely be able to overcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:54.300
his VERY FIRST DEFEAT against the Logia fruit&nbsp;
using Captain Smoker. Because if you remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.300 --> 00:06:01.260
Luffy only really struggled against opponents who&nbsp;
had Logia devil fruits because he simply could not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:08.400
hit them without knowing their elemental weakness&nbsp;
or having haki. But that’s literally not a problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.860
at all this time. Because once Luffy figures&nbsp;
out his haki-punches can hit Smoker, I don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:21.240
think there is any way the marine captain will&nbsp;
defeat Luffy. Which might mean that his bounty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:28.380
is WAY HIGHER heading into the Grand Line, which&nbsp;
might actually be a serious problem later on.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:34.320
At this point, I also think we should mention&nbsp;
that if Luffy knows haki he might also teach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:39.900
other members of the crew what he knows about&nbsp;
haki. Although, let’s be honest he’s probably not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:47.160
the greatest teacher, and he might just tell them&nbsp;
to figure it out on their own. But being around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:54.060
Luffy and seeing him use his haki abilities could&nbsp;
mean that characters like Zoro and Sanji figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.060 --> 00:07:02.340
out how to use haki much earlier in the story.&nbsp;
So a major overall power boost for the crew.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:07.800
Which takes us straight through the Alabasta&nbsp;
Saga to the eventual clash with the Warlord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:15.210
Crocodile. Now in the original story, Luffy&nbsp;
had to fight Crocodile THREE TIMES and there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:21.360
is no doubt that he would have died each time&nbsp;
if it weren’t for help from other people and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:26.520
ton of luck. But once again, haki is going&nbsp;
to COMPLETELY CHANGE these fights. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:32.880
the ability to hit Logia fruit users is just so&nbsp;
overpowered that Luffy should be able to deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:38.880
heavy damage to Crocodile right away. However,&nbsp;
this isn’t to say this fight would be easy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:44.460
especially since Luffy can only basically attack&nbsp;
from close range since he can’t stretch his body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:50.760
But Crocodile might also be super surprised&nbsp;
to find someone in this part of the world who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:56.700
can use haki, so really there’s no doubt in&nbsp;
my mind that Haki Luffy would find a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:01.860
win and save his friend Vivi’s kingdom.&nbsp;
Whew, so far so good for Haki Luffy, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:07.560
let’s see if he can actually survive against the&nbsp;
strongest characters like the one coming up next.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:12.660
And that’s because things are about to get&nbsp;
IMPOSSIBLY DIFFICULT when the crew flies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:18.060
up to Skypiea. It’s here that they come&nbsp;
face to face with the Lightning God Enel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:24.600
and Luffy is going to need a MASSIVE power&nbsp;
boost to take him down. Let’s explain why.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:33.780
In case you forgot, the ONLY WAY that Luffy was&nbsp;
originally able to defeat Enel was because of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:41.820
rubber body’s natural immunity to electricity. So&nbsp;
Enel’s main attacks were basically worthless. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:48.414
that advantage is out the window now, so at this&nbsp;
point, Luffy is in serious danger of getting one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.414 --> 00:08:54.660
shot by this electric powerhouse. And yes, just&nbsp;
like with Crocodile, Luffy can easily damage the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.660 --> 00:09:02.400
logia fruit user with his haki, but the problem&nbsp;
is getting close to Enel. It doesn’t matter how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:08.640
hard you punch if you get your heart fried&nbsp;
before you even get close enough to attack.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:13.620
However, Skypiea also is the PERFECT&nbsp;
OPPORTUNITY to introduce two new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:19.920
power ups for Haki Luffy. The first is&nbsp;
that we know Luffy is a haki prodigy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.840
which means he is super good at learning&nbsp;
the basic and advanced techniques,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:31.200
so I think that after pushing his observation haki&nbsp;
to the ABSOLUTE MAX when dodging Enel’s lighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:36.840
bolts it is quite realistic for him to awaken&nbsp;
advanced observation haki during this fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:43.560
And doing so would let him see a few seconds&nbsp;
into the future and give him a huge advantage.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:52.860
But if that isn’t enough, Luffy also gains another&nbsp;
HUGE BONUS by not being a devil fruit user. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:58.260
because in the original story we already saw&nbsp;
this Shandian warrior use Sea Prism Stone to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:03.240
help him nearly kill Enel. And normally Sea Prism&nbsp;
Stone drains the power of any devil fruit user,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:09.480
but now that Luffy is devil fruit free, he&nbsp;
could also somehow use these stones to gain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:16.080
an advantage against Enel. I can just imagine&nbsp;
Usopp somehow making him some Sea Stone brass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:22.140
knuckles so his punches would do extra damage&nbsp;
to devil fruit users. Which, let's be real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:27.120
is almost every single one of Luffy’s&nbsp;
fights. So with all this put together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:32.280
Haki Luffy should be able to&nbsp;
take down Enel and save Skypiea.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:39.360
But that’s not going to be enough to&nbsp;
save Haki Luffy from being COMPLETELY&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:45.000
OVERWHELMED by admiral Aokiji. In the&nbsp;
original story, he was completely washed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.580
by the admiral’s ice logia powers. And even&nbsp;
though Haki Luffy will probably land a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:56.400
blows, I still don’t think he comes close&nbsp;
to winning this fight. But we’ll see if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.020
that is still the case the next time that&nbsp;
Luffy fights an admiral in just a minute.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:05.880
However, while they eventually survived&nbsp;
that encounter with the admiral, Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:11.940
missing devil fruit will play a MAJOR ROLE in the&nbsp;
outcome of the next battle. Because after Robin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:19.500
was kidnapped by the government secret agents&nbsp;
Luffy needed not one but TWO MASSIVE POWER UPS&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:25.740
to defeat the leopard-man Rob Lucci. Those would&nbsp;
be Gear 2, which gave him an incredible boost in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:32.220
strength and speed, plus Gear Three which allowed&nbsp;
Luffy to increase the size of his fists. But again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:40.440
these upgrades are gone! So what is Luffy going&nbsp;
to do now? Well, there are a few options that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:48.480
could work. First, Haki Luffy could just be so&nbsp;
stupidly powerful that he beats Lucci without any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:55.620
upgrades. And honestly I think this is perfectly&nbsp;
valid, but if that doesn’t satisfy you then we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.620 --> 00:12:01.020
also consider that the entire crew is probably&nbsp;
stronger from seeing Luffy’s haki in action.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:08.400
So perhaps Zoro and Sanji defeat their opponents&nbsp;
much faster and then they can help their captain.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:15.600
Either way the crew should free Robin,&nbsp;
escape after a clash with Luffy’s Grandpa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:21.900
and then breeze through Thriller Bark to&nbsp;
reach Sabaody. But this is where things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:27.720
are going to go ABSOLUTELY CRAZY, and it&nbsp;
all starts by you hitting that nice red&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.300
subscribe button for more one&nbsp;
piece content just like this.

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:37.680
But here in Sabaody is where Haki Luffy will&nbsp;
truly be tested for the first time. And we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:43.680
could assume that Luffy’s advanced observation&nbsp;
haki will help him make sure this mermaid never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:49.680
gets kidnapped in the first place. However, that&nbsp;
takes a lot of the fun out of this arc, so let’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:56.160
imagine that Luffy still punches a World Noble&nbsp;
which means that Admiral Kizaru and the cyborg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:03.180
Pacificstas come to hunt them down. So here is&nbsp;
where Haki Luffy is really going to shine. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:09.720
if we are assuming he started his journey with&nbsp;
haki skill as good as right after the time skip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:17.100
then he should be able to crush the Pacificsta no&nbsp;
problem, right? I mean just look at what he did to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:22.740
this one before they left for Fishman Island. Plus&nbsp;
he’s grown stronger through all of his fights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:28.440
so I honestly don’t see the Pacifistas being&nbsp;
that much of a problem for the Straw Hats.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:33.780
Which means we have to ask if they would still&nbsp;
need to be separated by the Warlord Bartholemew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:39.540
Kuma? I mean, I think Luffy at this point&nbsp;
might put up a better fight against Kizaru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:45.900
but he still wouldn’t be able to take him down&nbsp;
alone. So if Rayleigh is there to hold off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:51.540
admiral there is a great chance the crew&nbsp;
could escape together. On the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:57.480
if Kuma really was determined to send them&nbsp;
all over the world there is nothing Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:03.120
could do about it at this point. Haki isn’t&nbsp;
going to stop the awesome pushing power. Plus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:07.920
they wouldn’t be able to go to Fishman&nbsp;
Island yet without coating the ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:14.280
so let’s imagine that the story follows its normal&nbsp;
path and they all get separated like normal.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:20.580
Now before we see that HUGE IMPACT THAT Luffy is&nbsp;
going to make at Marineford, but first I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:26.040
his path to getting to this epic war would go&nbsp;
pretty similarly to the original. Although on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:30.960
Island of Women, the pirate Empress Boa Hancock&nbsp;
might fall in love right from the start because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:37.980
of Luffy’s overwhelming conqueror’s haki and&nbsp;
kindness. But Impel Down wouldn’t change all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:43.200
that much. He still wouldn’t be able to punch&nbsp;
the venomous warden, so no big changes here.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:51.240
However, when Luffy drops into Marineford, I could&nbsp;
definitely see him charging into the war with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:58.740
full conqueror’s haki blazing. And can you just&nbsp;
imagine the insanity of an entire battlefield of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:05.040
marines and pirates turning to see this madman&nbsp;
dropping in from the sky?! A bunch of the weaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:10.260
enemies would probably drop unconscious on&nbsp;
the spot, and it might even force an admiral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:16.680
to come after Luffy right away because he is&nbsp;
an unknown threat at this point. And speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:22.980
of the admirals, they are honestly some of the&nbsp;
few characters who can stop Haki Luffy at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:29.700
point. Them plus Garp, the Fleet Admiral Sengoku,&nbsp;
or the world’s strongest swordsman Mihawk are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:38.700
truly their only hope. Honestly, I don’t even&nbsp;
think Doflamingo could stop Haki-Luffy with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:44.880
current power level. So Luffy would definitely&nbsp;
square off with someone like Kizaru. But instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:51.720
of being easily sniped like in the original war,&nbsp;
Luffy should puts up a decent fight because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:57.420
his advanced observation and the fact that he&nbsp;
can actually hit the light logia fruit user.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:05.040
Which might mean that the Whitebeard pirates&nbsp;
stand a WAY BETTER chance of succeeding in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:10.860
rescuing Ace. Because if Luffy is taking the&nbsp;
attention of an admiral all by himself that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:15.960
means the strongest allied pirates like the&nbsp;
Emperor Whitebeard, Marco the Phoenix, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:21.840
escaped prisoners like Crocodile and the fishman&nbsp;
Jinbe would get much closer to rescuing Ace.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:30.360
But sadly, just because Luffy is way stronger&nbsp;
that doesn’t mean he is strong enough to win a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:35.640
one on one with an admiral, so let’s imagine&nbsp;
he gets away and frees Ace just like in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:41.220
original story. Hold on, wait, that just means&nbsp;
we are heading straight to Donut Ace again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:47.700
right? Well, let’s find out. Because with Luffy’s&nbsp;
Advanced Observation he should be able to sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:52.980
Admiral Akainu coming and at least dodge his&nbsp;
fiery magma fist. But he honestly wouldn’t be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:59.700
able to run away forever, and even if he is able&nbsp;
to block a magma punch then it would most likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:04.740
send him flying across the battlefield. And with&nbsp;
Whitebeard suffering his normal heart attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:10.068
that unfortunately leaves Ace to&nbsp;
once again get killed by Akainu.

00:17:10.068 --> 00:17:14.040
*Fake cry.* Almost Ace. You&nbsp;
almost made it this time.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.440
So with the major turning point over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:21.120
let’s assume Shanks arrives to stop&nbsp;
the war and Luffy escapes like normal.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:31.860
Which gives us one MAJOR QUESTION to ask.&nbsp;
Would there need to be a timeskip in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:36.840
scenario? Because if you remember Rayleigh&nbsp;
came to train Luffy with the main goal of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:42.240
teaching him hakiBut since Luffy already&nbsp;
is well on his way to being a haki master,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:47.640
is that even necessary? Well, honestly I think&nbsp;
yes. Because in our version of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:52.980
the rest of the crew is still separated and they&nbsp;
could definitely use time to train. Plus I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:59.940
it would be a huge waste for Luffy to not train&nbsp;
with one of the few legitimate haki masters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:04.620
so let’s assume that Rayleigh does train Luffy for&nbsp;
the normal timeskip, but instead of learning basic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:11.100
haki, Rayleigh puts him through a BRUTAL training&nbsp;
regiment that helps him master Advanced Armament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:18.420
and possibly also advanced conqueror’s.&nbsp;
Although I must admit that Luffy probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:25.980
wouldn’t master this last one yet because as we&nbsp;
know, haki blooms most during intense battle.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:33.060
However, all this means that after the timeskip,&nbsp;
Haki Luffy and the straw hats are way overpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:38.400
for the rest of the New World. Honestly I could&nbsp;
see this version of Luffy one-shotting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:43.680
post-time skip opponents like this roided out&nbsp;
fishman, this gas man, and the pink flamingo.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:48.000
Which just leaves Luffy to fight against the&nbsp;
Emperor’s Big Mom and Kaido. And during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:53.160
Whole Cake Island Arc we would get one of the most&nbsp;
interesting clashes against Big Mom’s strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:58.680
son, Katakuri. Because for much of this original&nbsp;
fight Katakuri didn’t respect Luffy as a fighter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:04.620
And for good reason. Katakuri was clearly stronger&nbsp;
with his superior armament haki AND future sight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:10.200
haki. But in this version of the story, there&nbsp;
is no doubt that Luffy has the upper hand. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:16.680
I wonder if Katakuri would really even go so far&nbsp;
as to fight Luffy. Or would they even clash at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:21.240
all? I mean Luffy might just be able to kick him&nbsp;
off the ship which would allow the crew to Coup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:26.760
De Burst away on the Sunny. Luffy might also have&nbsp;
a longer clash with Big Mom during this arc, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:35.940
since his real goal was to just rescue Sanji and&nbsp;
leave, I don’t think they’d go all out just yet.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:44.280
So onto Wano-kuni and the BIGGEST CONTROVERSY YET.&nbsp;
Because this is the scene of Luffy's biggest test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:51.120
against the Strongest Creature in the Sea, Kadio.&nbsp;
And honestly, I’m going to drop a hot take here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:57.240
because if Luffy is facing Kaido while already&nbsp;
having a ton of experience with Advanced Armament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:03.780
haki, future sight, and he understands the basics&nbsp;
of Advanced Conquerors, then I truly don’t see how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:10.020
Kaido can beat him. Because Luffy was beat down&nbsp;
so much during his original fight with Kaido,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:14.340
and it wasn’t until he learned advanced&nbsp;
conquerors that he was actually able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:19.620
do any real damage to the King of the Beasts.&nbsp;
And although Luffy even had to awaken Gear 5 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:26.160
eventually beat the oni-dragon, by that point he&nbsp;
was already exhausted. So if Luffy has basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:34.560
his strongest abilities from the very start of&nbsp;
the battle, then I think his insane will power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:39.900
durability, and overall haki mastery will&nbsp;
lead him to defeat Kaido once and for all.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:49.260
BUT… AND THIS IS A BIG BUT! That leaves us&nbsp;
with a SUPER IMPORTANT question. Without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:55.320
unlocking Gear 5 can Luffy still become&nbsp;
Joy Boy and bring freedom to the world?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.320 --> 00:21:00.840
Well, honestly I think no. I mean it was pretty&nbsp;
clear in the original story that it was only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:07.500
after Luffy awakened Gear 5 that this giant&nbsp;
elephant officially recognized him as Joy Boy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:12.960
So without his legendary Nika devil fruit, it&nbsp;
just isn’t possible. But, remember that little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:18.180
promise Shanks made to Luffy at the start of this&nbsp;
video. Let’s discuss that more in just a moment.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:24.660
Because from here, I think Luffy has a pretty&nbsp;
clear path to finding Laugh Tale and becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:29.100
pirate king. And we know he doesn’t need&nbsp;
to be Joy Boy to find Laught Tale since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:35.100
Roger was able to do it. So the question&nbsp;
would be could Luffy still use whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:40.920
treasure was left at Laugh Tale and go on to&nbsp;
save the world without being Joy Boy? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:46.140
we don’t really know, but this could also be&nbsp;
the perfect time for Luffy and Shanks to meet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:50.940
and if Shanks has been holding onto the Nika&nbsp;
fruit all this time then he could very well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:57.000
offer it to Luffy if he truly believes&nbsp;
Luffy is destined to become Joy Boy.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:02.700
Now, I don’t know if Haki Luffy would all of a&nbsp;
sudden want to eat a devil fruit, and even if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:07.500
he did it might take him some time to awaken it,&nbsp;
but if this is a required step to save the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:15.060
I could see Luffy doing it. Which might be a&nbsp;
bit disappointing since he came all this way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:20.760
with just his haki, but since he’s already&nbsp;
eating one, why don’t we make things EVEN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:26.520
CRAZIER by giving him a SECOND DEVIL fruit&nbsp;
as well?! WHICH SOUNDS COMPLETELY WILD,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:31.680
but can you imagine if Luffy had two devil&nbsp;
fruits at the start of the story? So if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:35.820
want to know which powers would combine&nbsp;
with his original fruit best and how it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:39.540
would COMPLETELY CHANGE his adventure,&nbsp;
you can watch that video right here.

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:51.600
Shanks for watching and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:51.778
###

